From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Maria Blasco <josep.maria.blasco@epbcn.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:51:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cmdhandler: command environments (ADDRESS) written in Rexx

New extension package extensions/cmdhandler (cmdhandler.cpp + cmdhandler.cls),
only public native API: .CommandHandler~register(name, object) makes an
object whose class inherits .CommandHandler (a mixin class, COMMAND
abstract; required) an ADDRESS environment; each command is sent as
object~command(command, .CommandContext), the result becomes RC.  The context
gives WITH INPUT / OUTPUT / ERROR and the variables of the code that issued
the command; ~raiseError / ~raiseFailure; SYNTAX errors reach the caller.
Registrations are per interpreter instance, as the environments themselves:
.local~CommandHandlers (name -> object) and .local~CommandContext.
Native: libcmdhandler; WASM: embedded package (PackageManager table), .cls in
bin / bin-node / bin-web.  Tests: wasm/tests/cmdhandler.rex (33 checks, also
in qualify-node-cli.sh and web-api.py); extensions/cmdhandler/tests/
instances.cpp (two instances in one process, native).  Portable, not part
of the posted RFE.
